---

The indexer (polyphony-xdg) began as a fork of TxPipe's Scrolls
(https://github.com/txpipe/scrolls, Apache-2.0) and has since been
substantially rewritten; portions of the original remain. It is built on the
gasket staged-pipeline framework (https://github.com/construkts/gasket-rs,
Apache-2.0).

Metaprotocol handling builds on the ord project
(https://github.com/ordinals/ord, CC0-1.0) and the ordinals crate; the dunes
implementation is a Dogecoin adaptation of the runes protocol machinery from
those projects. Dogecoin block decoding uses a maintained fork of rust-bitcoin
(https://github.com/maestro-org/rust-bitcoin, upstream
https://github.com/rust-bitcoin/rust-bitcoin, MIT/CC0), and the API layer's
Dogecoin address handling uses rust-dogecoin
(https://github.com/tobin-crypto/rust-dogecoin, a rust-bitcoin derivative,
pinned by revision).

compressor-xdg's P2P handshake and the Dogecoin genesis constants derive in
part from metashrew (https://github.com/sandshrewmetaprotocols/metashrew,
MIT).

The stack uses maintained forks of the TiKV Rust client, published under the
maestro-org GitHub organisation (Apache-2.0).
